## Available in this candidate

- The dependency-free native `qiongli` CLI, embedded academic skills, and
  deterministic Lite content materialization.
- The native desktop manager and `qiongli ui --startup-check`. The displayed
  window and accessibility evidence remain external publication gates.
- The native Lite MCP server with its bounded public tool set.
- Receipt-backed Qiongli-managed source registration for Codex local and
  Claude Code local.
- Acceptance from freshly extracted bytes outside the checkout with an
  empty runtime PATH; users do not need Rust, Python, Node.js, Cargo, npm, or
  pip.

## Required host actions

Qiongli writes only its documented managed payload, local plugin source, and
registration entries. Codex and Claude Code still own plugin installation or
enablement, trust, cache, and reload state. The user or host must complete
those actions after Qiongli reports `install-or-enable-plugin`.

## Diagnose, remove, and rollback boundary

- Preview verifies the complete candidate and performs no mutation.
- Verify diagnoses only receipt-backed Qiongli-managed payload, source, and
  registration state; it does not diagnose client-owned cache or enablement.
- Remove verifies the complete receipt chain first, requires the exact
  filesystem and client-config approvals, and removes registration, source,
  and payload in reverse order.
- A fresh apply failure compensates only fresh earlier Qiongli mutations.
  Existing healthy state is replayed and is never removed as compensation.
- Drift, ambiguous ownership, or a partial removal fails closed with
  recovery-required evidence. Qiongli does not delete unverified state.

## Not included in Alpha.1

- Full MCP, executing agents, ToolHost, and full orchestrator execution target
  Alpha.2 and are unavailable in this candidate.
- Claude Desktop, Codex Desktop or ChatGPT Marketplace bypass, cloud or web
  execution, and public Marketplace distribution are unavailable.
- Updater and managed upgrade behavior, cross-target packages, OS signing or
  notarization, SBOM, provenance, and stable update metadata are not claimed.

